            "typeClass": "compound",
            "value": [
              {
                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "<p>During the COVID-19 pandemic, issues of (civic) (ir)responsibility were raised virtually every time people broke immobility rules. I have investigated the relationship between mobility and (ir)responsibility by focussing on the creative modalities through which (some) people in Paris circumvented mobility restrictions. Here I provide the transcripts of the interviews carried out between November and December 2022.<br>These interviews have been conducted as part of the following: MOBILISE project - Marie Skłodowska-Curie grant agreement no. 101024492: ‘MOBILISE: Stay home: Emergency, (im)mobility, and the liberal subject’, and included in the following article: COVID-19 and (ir)responsible mobility:  Reading counter-practices through Derrida, submitted in Open Research Europe, in the collection ‘The Future of Democracy’.</p>"
                }
              },
              {
                "dsDescriptionValue": {
